## Architecture Overview

Every runtime composes the same **transport-independent services** and **injectable contracts** instead of duplicating business rules per platform:

```text
                        SHARED UI (Svelte 5 + UnoCSS)
                    packages/frontend/{ui, features}
                                    │
                                    ▼
                   TRANSPORT-INDEPENDENT TS CLIENT
                         packages/application
                    (depends only on @product/contracts)
                                    │
                                    ▼
                   INJECTABLE INFRASTRUCTURE ADAPTERS
         packages/infrastructure/{memory, http, tauri, wasm, extension}
             │               │              │               │
             ▼               ▼              ▼               ▼
         apps/web      apps/desktop    apps/mobile    apps/extension
       (Rust Axum       (Tauri v2       (Tauri v2       (WXT MV3
      Alpine binary)     Desktop)        Mobile)        Browsers)
             │               │              │               │
             └───────────────┴──────┬───────┴───────────────┘
                                    ▼
                        THIN RUST TRANSPORT ADAPTERS
                     rust/adapters/{axum, tauri, wasm}
                                    │
                                    ▼
                    TRANSPORT-INDEPENDENT RUST CORE
              rust/crates/{domain, contracts, services, storage, sync}
```

### Core Design Principles

1. **Zero-dependency contracts (`rust/crates/contracts`, `packages/contracts`):** Wire shapes, error taxonomies, and capability interfaces depend on nothing else in the workspace so clients and tests compile ahead of any runtime.
2. **One service layer, many doors (`rust/crates/services`):** Validation and business rules execute through `ProductServices` (single-door `dispatch` + typed operations). `rust/adapters/{axum,tauri,wasm}` only translate HTTP, Tauri IPC, or WASM payloads.
3. **Injectable TypeScript infrastructure (`packages/infrastructure/*`):** Every adapter accepts its low-level runtime primitive (`fetch`, `invoke`, `sendMessage`, lazy WASM loader) as a parameter and provides safe preview fallbacks (such as degrading cleanly outside a Tauri WebView in browser previews).
4. **Svelte 5 presentation stays platform-agnostic (`packages/frontend/*`):** Components consume contracts and callbacks—never Tauri IPC, `chrome.*`/`browser.*`, or raw `fetch`.
5. **Private by default:** Every internal Cargo crate (`publish.workspace = true` → `false`) and npm package (`"private": true`) blocks accidental publication until explicitly opted out.

